=======================================================================
 test_poisson_nonconvex - recovering a nonconvex polygon outline
=======================================================================

WHAT THIS IS

  A stress test of how the 2D driver recovers a NONCONVEX outline.

  The driver connects the Poisson points into a convex hull Delaunay
  mesh, then clips it: it triangulates the polygon, interpolates a
  marker onto the mesh and deletes every element whose centroid falls
  outside. A notch narrower than the sample spacing h gets no sample
  points inside it, so the clip cannot reproduce it.

  These tests locate where that happens and measure what it looks
  like. They push the algorithm past the point where it works ON
  PURPOSE, so a degraded mesh is an expected result, not a failure.

QUICK START

  ./run_nonconvex_tests.sh  [path-to-lagrit]

  then open, in a web browser,

      logs/summary.html

  That one page has the tally, the results table and, for every deck,
  its notes, its full report and a picture.

  Requires: LaGriT, Python 3 (standard library only), a POSIX shell.

