-----------------------------------------------------------------------
THE SHAPE, AND WHY h IS THE KNOB
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  make_sawtooth.py builds a long box with a sawtooth top: valleys at a
  fixed height, peaks growing left to right under a linear, power or
  exponential envelope, valleys at both ends. Vertices run
  counter-clockwise, as the driver requires.

  Recovery depends on the ratio

      tooth half width / h

  The obvious experiment, narrower and taller teeth, does not work: a
  tall thin tooth has a sharp apex, and the driver refuses any polygon
  with a vertex angle under 9 degrees before the sampler runs (nc09
  keeps one such polygon on purpose). So the geometry is held fixed at
  safe angles and h is varied instead.

  Regenerate any polygon exactly from its sidecar:

      python3 make_sawtooth.py --out saw_safe --from-json saw_safe.json

