-----------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDINGS (latest run, regenerated polygons)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. Recovery holds while tooth half width / h >= 1 (nc01-nc04: 0.00 %
     mismatch) and degrades below it (nc05 0.67 %, nc06 2.48 %, nc07
     6.06 %). 0.5 % still separates the two, with less margin than in
     the first run.

  2. Degradation now ADDS area where triangles bridge the notches as
     well as losing some from the teeth (nc05: all overhang). On the
     old polygons it mostly lost area. The deck notes have both runs.

  3. nc06 is a KNOWN failure (documented in its deck; nothing to fix
     to keep the suite green). One triangle with its centroid outside
     the polygon survives the clip, which the driver's nonconvex
     warning says cannot happen. Measured Oct 6: centroid (18.79,
     1.78), 0.167 outside the polygon = 0.26 x its shortest edge, so a
     real clip miss, not rounding: a triangle bridging the notch above
     the valley at x = 18.75.

     Not interpolate/map: it tags a centroid outside the polygon's
     triangulation with max+1 = 2, and the clip deletes "gt 1". The
     two causes left, and how to tell them apart:
       a) triangulate/counterclockwise covers the notch, so the
          centroid counts as inside. Run diag_triangulate.lgi, then
            python3 check_recovery.py saw_safe.poly diag_triangulate.inp
          Any overhang confirms it.
       b) smooth;recon AFTER the clip moved nodes or flipped edges.
          logs/nc06_h1p0.recovery lists the triangle's three nodes and
          whether each is on the outline; a node off it points here.

  4. Notch tips go missing at FINER h, not coarser: saw_sharp has
     58/63 vertices as mesh nodes at h 0.3 (nc08) but 55/63 at h 0.1
     (nc12); saw_edge_admit 51/63 at h 0.1. The area cost is tiny
     (<= 0.04 %), but it points at the sampler, not at h.

  5. nc12 is a KNOWN failure since Oct 18 2026 (user accepted), after
     the Poisson driver switched to a binned vertex sort before
     connect (poi_driver.f): 2 triangles with centroids
     just outside the polygon (<= 6e-3 x the shortest edge) at the
     reflex corners (13.33, 1) and (22.5, 1), where no vertex was
     placed. Each has one vertex off the outline: the smooth;recon
     passes after the clip, which depend on vertex order, made them.
     Same cause as nc06's explanation 2. Possible follow-up (offered,
     not started): run the clip again after the smoothing, or clip
     last.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
ADDING A TEST
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Copy an nc*.lgi deck. The runner reads three header lines:

      # polygon : <file>.poly
      # h       : <value>
      # expect  : recovered | degraded | error

  and a deck expecting an error may add

      # reason  : <text that must appear in the ERROR message>

  A deck with a documented failure adds

      # known    : <text from the HARD line it fails with>
      # expected : <one line: what happens, and where it is explained>

  It then reports KNOWN instead of FAIL, but only if EVERY hard check
  that failed contains that text, so a new, different fault still
  FAILs.

  A deck with no expect line FAILS, so a new test cannot go unjudged.
  The deck must dump its mesh to out_<deck>.inp.

